From: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: suniv-di: raise MIN_LUMA_TH against stray pixels

The de-interlacer (0048) never set DI_PARA, so it ran on the reset
values (CHROMA_DIFF_TH 5, SPATIAL_TH2 10, AVG_LUMA_SHIFTER 6,
MIN_LUMA_TH 9). With those, the motion path puts isolated wrong pixels on
the interpolated lines: 0, or about twice the neighbourhood, where the
fields, the previous frame and the vertical average all agree.

Measured on the F1C200s over 10 frames (isolated outliers, and luma PSNR
against the true progressive frame of a 50 fps test pattern):

  MIN_LUMA_TH   film   composite camera   test pattern PSNR
   9 (reset)     62         296              36.90 dB
  20              6         115              36.78 dB
  25              1          28              36.69 dB
  30              3          43              36.58 dB
  255             0           -              30.70 dB (combing)

The flag buffer (cleared or not, twice the stride) and the other fields
made no useful difference. Program DI_PARA on every job, with MIN_LUMA_TH
25 and the manual's defaults for the rest.
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/suniv-di/suniv-di.c b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/suniv-di/suniv-di.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/suniv-di/suniv-di.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/suniv-di/suniv-di.c
@@ -58,6 +58,22 @@
 #define SUNIV_DI_OUT_ADDR1		0x64
 #define SUNIV_DI_FLAG_ADDR		0x70
 #define SUNIV_DI_PARA			0x80
+#define SUNIV_DI_PARA_CHROMA_DIFF_TH(v)		((v) << 24)
+#define SUNIV_DI_PARA_SPATIAL_TH2(v)		((v) << 16)
+#define SUNIV_DI_PARA_AVG_LUMA_SHIFTER(v)	((v) << 8)
+#define SUNIV_DI_PARA_MIN_LUMA_TH(v)		((v) << 0)
+
+/*
+ * The motion parameters: the manual's defaults, except MIN_LUMA_TH. At its
+ * default of 9 the motion path puts isolated wrong pixels (0, or about
+ * twice the neighbourhood) on the interpolated lines: ~6 per frame on film,
+ * ~30 on the composite camera. 25 removes ~90-98% of them for 0.2 dB on a
+ * fast-moving test pattern; 40 and more start to lose motion (combing).
+ */
+#define SUNIV_DI_PARA_VALUE	(SUNIV_DI_PARA_CHROMA_DIFF_TH(5) | \
+				 SUNIV_DI_PARA_SPATIAL_TH2(10) | \
+				 SUNIV_DI_PARA_AVG_LUMA_SHIFTER(6) | \
+				 SUNIV_DI_PARA_MIN_LUMA_TH(25))
 
 #define SUNIV_DI_MIN_WIDTH		32U
 #define SUNIV_DI_MIN_HEIGHT		32U
@@ -191,6 +207,7 @@
 	suniv_di_write(dev, SUNIV_DI_OUT_LS0, ctx->dst_fmt.bytesperline / 4);
 	suniv_di_write(dev, SUNIV_DI_OUT_LS1, ctx->dst_fmt.bytesperline / 4);
 	suniv_di_write(dev, SUNIV_DI_FLAG_LS, ALIGN(ctx->src_fmt.width, 4) / 4);
+	suniv_di_write(dev, SUNIV_DI_PARA, SUNIV_DI_PARA_VALUE);
 
 	cur = vb2_dma_contig_plane_dma_addr(&src->vb2_buf, 0);
 	pre = vb2_dma_contig_plane_dma_addr(&prev->vb2_buf, 0);
